@[expose] public section

/-!
# The proof map of the central-charge-eight construction

This file records the complete logical structure of the manuscript
`c8_expanded_20260929/haagerup_c8_expanded.tex` (Appendices A–K) as a
kernel-checked deduction.  Every intermediate claim of the manuscript is a
node (a proposition about the actual objects `U ⊂ B ⊂ H`, `Rep(U)`, the
boundary category `𝓕`, the net `𝒩_U`, ...).  Every arrow is one of

* `C_…` — a **certificate input**: an exact finite identity of the lattice
  construction (Appendix `sec:ledger`), accepted as input by the manuscript;
* `E_…` — an **external theorem** from the literature, specialized to the
  objects at hand;
* `L_…` — a **manuscript lemma**: an argument given in the manuscript.

Theorems `prop_mainproper`, `thm_main_net`, `thm_claim_main` derive the three
main results of the manuscript from these inputs.  The derivation checks that
the arrows compose: no step is missing, and no main result uses an input that
is not listed.  It does *not* by itself verify any arrow.

The mathematical content of the `L_…` arrows is verified in the concrete
modules of `HaagerupIzumi.C8` (see `README.md`); each field's docstring names
the Lean theorem formalizing its core argument and the hypotheses that remain.
The node propositions are deliberately opaque here: their concrete versions
(vertex-algebra closure data, fusion rings, twist multisets, characters) live
in those modules.
-/

